# Bureau: environment. Nothing here is required: a hub started with no token
# makes its own boss token in data/boss-token and prints a one-time link that
# signs you in (README, "Run it"). Copy this file to .env only to change a setting.
# BUREAU_BOSS_TOKEN=               # your own boss token instead of the hub's: only this token acts as the boss
# BUREAU_TOKEN=                    # the old shared agent token, for hubs that still need it. With only this set, the hub runs in legacy mode. A placeholder stops the boot
PORT=8100
# HOST=127.0.0.1                # the default: this machine only. To serve others, set 0.0.0.0, or :: on hosts that want IPv6
# BUREAU_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=       # comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the API. Same origin always works
# BUREAU_ALLOW_INSECURE_LOCAL=1 # local demos only: start with no real token, on loopback
# BUREAU_PUBLIC_URL=            # a hub on a server: its https address. Leave it out for a hub on your own computer
# Sign-in (docs/protocol.md, "Sign-in"). With OMAKO, nothing to set: Sign in with OMAKO in the
# setup guide or Settings pairs the hub (or, on the server: node hub/tools/omako.js pair).
# With another issuer, register a client there with the redirect <BUREAU_PUBLIC_URL>/auth/callback and set:
# BUREAU_OIDC_ISSUER=https://id.omako.dev   # or any OAuth 2.1 / OpenID issuer
# BUREAU_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=                    # the dashboard's client at that issuer
# BUREAU_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=                # its secret; leave out for a public PKCE client
# BUREAU_OIDC_OWNERS=you@example.com        # who owns this hub: emails or the issuer's subject ids
# BUREAU_OIDC_SCOPE=bureau                  # the scope an agent's token must carry
# BUREAU_OIDC_CLI_CLIENT_ID=bureau-cli      # the CLI's client at that issuer (bureau login)
# BUREAU_POKES=                 # optional: outbound wake-up pokes (the summoner), JSON array of subscriptions, e.g.
#   [{"url":"https://…","headers":{"X-Key":"…"},"events":["task.review"],"filter":{"gate":"critic"}}]
#   events may include "work.waiting" (standing-work bell, sweep-driven): add
#   "unless_seen":{"agents":["name"],"within_min":10} and "every_min":30 to keep it polite.
# BUREAU_SWEEP_MS=60000         # sweep cadence (lease expiry + standing-work bell)
# BUREAU_RESERVATION_TTL_MIN=30 # minutes a cowork worker's reservation holds before the pool may take the mission
# BUREAU_TZ=UTC                 # the time zone stats count days in when the caller gives none (an IANA name, e.g. Europe/Paris). The dashboard always sends its own
# BUREAU_DATA_DIR=./data            # state.json location
# BUREAU_STORE=sqlite               # keep the state in data/bureau.db instead (Node 22.13+, see UPGRADING.md)
# BUREAU_HUB_ID=                    # SQLite: the hub's id; a database made by another hub is refused
# BUREAU_BACKUP_INTERVAL_MS=3600000 # rolling state.json.bak.N cadence (hourly)
# BUREAU_BACKUP_KEEP=24             # rolling backups kept
# BUREAU_DAILY_KEEP=7               # daily snapshots kept
# The nightly off-server backup (SQLite store only, docs/restore.md). Off until the
# first four are all set. Put them on the server by script, never through a chat.
# BUREAU_BACKUP_PUBLIC_KEY=         # x25519:..., printed by `bureau backup keygen` on the Mac. Not a secret
# BUREAU_NEXTCLOUD_URL=             # https://your.nextcloud, where the copies go (WebDAV)
# BUREAU_NEXTCLOUD_USER=            # the Nextcloud user
# BUREAU_NEXTCLOUD_PASSWORD=        # an app password for Bureau alone, revocable on its own
# BUREAU_NEXTCLOUD_DIR=Bureau-backup  # the folder; each hub writes under <folder>/<hub id>/
# BUREAU_OPERATORS=                 # who runs this server (emails): they alone see the backup's state. Default: BUREAU_OIDC_OWNERS
# BUREAU_BRAIN_DIR=./brain          # knowledge git repo location
# BUREAU_WORK_DIR=./work            # work store: open missions' evidence, plain files, deleted when a mission closes
